@startuml
|User|
start

:User logs into application;

:User navigates to workout dashboard;

:User selects "Add Workout" view;

|System|

if (User has logged workouts?) then (Yes)
  :Retrieve user's full workout history;

  :Analyze muscle groups targeted in previous workouts;

  :Calculate frequency countfor each muscle group;

  :Sort muscle groups byfrequency (ascending);

  if (Least-worked group rested at least 2 days?) then (Yes)
    :\nGenerate suggestion notification for that muscle group;

    :Display notification to user: \n"We suggest targeting [Muscle Group] today!";
  else (No)
    if (More muscle groups to evaluate?) then (Yes)
      :Move to next least-frequent muscle group;

      :Check if new candidate has rested at least 2 days;

      :Generate suggestion for valid candidate group;

      :Display notification: \n"We suggest targeting [Muscle Group] today!";
    else (No)
      :Display fallback message:\n "All groups are active — choose freely!";
    endif
  endif
else (No)
  :Display message:\n "Log workouts to receive muscle group suggestions";
endif

|User|

:User reviews suggestion and proceeds to add workout;

|System|

:Log selected workout to user history;

stop
@enduml